    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10282" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπαρα-σκευάζομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prepare oneself in
				turn, arm on both sides,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				10.29
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀλλήλοις ὡς ἐς μάχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later, in 
				Act.
			, <i>instigate in return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ ἐναντιωθῆναί σφισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					38.14
				</span></i>
			.</div>
